  "summary": "A personal Subscription Tracker: add, edit, and delete subscriptions with Service, Category (Entertainment/Productivity/Utilities), numeric Monthly cost, and Status (Active by default). Cancel sets a subscription to Cancelled and Reactivate reverses it. Filter the list to Active/Cancelled/All and see the summed Active monthly spend in EUR. Data persists in localStorage across refreshes; required input is validated and malformed stored data is ignored.",
  "implemented_features": [
    "Add subscription with service, category dropdown, numeric monthly cost (defaults to Active)",
    "Edit an existing subscription",
    "Delete a subscription",
    "Cancel (Active -> Cancelled) and Reactivate (Cancelled -> Active)",
    "Filter the collection by status (All / Active / Cancelled)",
    "Summed Active monthly spend displayed in EUR",
    "Persistence in localStorage across refreshes",
    "Validation of required service and numeric monthly cost",
    "Recovery from malformed persisted storage data"
  ],
  "assumptions": [
    "Currency is EUR as stated; costs are formatted with the Euro currency and the active spend sums only Active subscriptions.",
    "The idea says 'Filter to Active'; I also expose Cancelled and All filters as a natural category/state narrowing without changing the required Active filter behavior.",
    "Edit allows changing service, category, and cost but not status; status changes only via Cancel/Reactivate to keep those operations explicit.",
    "No edit-by-duplicate suppression was implied; adding two subscriptions with the same service is allowed since subscriptions are not described as unique.",
    "Storage failures (quota/unavailable) are swallowed so the UI keeps working in-memory rather than crashing."
  ],
